# Swapping `int*` contents vs `int**` pointers in C

## The Two Functions

```c
#include <stdio.h>

// Function 1: Swaps the VALUES that two pointers point to
void swap_int_ptrs(int* a, int* b) {
    if (a == NULL || b == NULL) return;

    int temp = *a;  // Dereference to get the value
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}

// Function 2: Swaps the POINTERS themselves
void swap_int_ptrs_ptrs(int** a, int** b) {
    if (a == NULL || b == NULL) return;

    int* temp = *a;  // Dereference once to get the pointer
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}
```

